# Shell scripts and container entrypoints MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. Those files are then bind-mounted into Linux
# containers (e.g. camera-simulator mounts scripts/publish-streams.sh into the
# ffmpeg image), where `sh` fails on the trailing \r with
# "set: line 2: illegal option -". `git archive` applies the same conversion,
# so deployment tarballs inherit the problem.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert.
*.mp4           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.pt            binary
*.engine        binary
*.onnx          binary
